Caveats that survive this run:
  - momentum and baseaxis differ in TWO ways, the axis and its radius policy; one run
    cannot separate them (see PREREG).
  - the pre-registered N=12 vanilla control still does not exist, so probe-vs-vanilla
    cannot separate 'mechanism works' from 'four fewer Gaussian explorers'.
  - absolute accuracies are depressed by the unfixed \boxed{} extractor bug. It is
    common-mode across arms, so paired comparisons hold and absolute numbers do not.
